Description: NVIDIA Spark GRUB KHO configuration
 Add kho=off to the kernel command line to disable Kexec HandOver. The
 kernel sets CONFIG_KEXEC_HANDOVER_ENABLE_DEFAULT, so KHO reserves scratch
 memory on every boot. With CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=0 that reservation stays
 marked MIGRATE_CMA while unaccounted in CmaTotal, so long-term pins such as
 ibv_reg_mr must migrate off those pages and fail with ENOMEM under memory
 pressure, which breaks NCCL and RoCE workloads.

